 "rule": "Rule PB(k): in the seed step, the MC refinement of a candidate (MC then variance stage) has a stall check after k strict-cost evaluations with no strict gain of its best cost: the hit ratio of the running best (the first lowest-cost orientation) is evaluated once; at 0.95 or more or under 0.80 the refinement stops and the check is its final evaluation (counted); else it goes on (the check counted as one evaluation) and checks again k evaluations after the next gain. It replaces PH(3000). Forms PB(1000) and PB(500). CMA fits, the five candidates, the 0.95 stop, the seed test 0.80, rules G1 and G2b and the grid search are unchanged. Arm JB = arm J (step 14) with PB(k).",
